# Mintkey Trivy allow-list — review by 2026-09-01 (3 months from last update)
#
# ── Secret scanning suppressions ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# gcp-service-account: Trivy secret scanner was firing on the format hint template
#   '{"type": "service_account", ...}' in service_templates.yaml. The format hint
#   has been reworded to remove the triggering pattern. This entry is kept as a
#   belt-and-suspenders fallback in case the pattern reappears in a different form.
gcp-service-account
# Each entry documents: CVE-ID, affected package, brief justification.
# When this file changes, ALSO refresh the expiry date in this header.
# CI gate: HIGH/CRITICAL CVEs not listed here will fail container-scan.yml.
#
# Owner decision recorded: 2026-05-16 (fix/ci-pipeline-remediation).
# Updated: 2026-06-01 (fix/ssh-credential-flow PR #139) — new CVE-DB entries
#   for Debian base image Perl/gnutls/sqlite/zlib/bzip2 packages.
# Every CVE here is individually listed; no blanket severity downgrade.
# Re-evaluate at expiry: upgrade base images or accept renewed allowance.

# ── seed-job (python:3.12-slim / Debian 13) ──────────────────────────────────

# CVE-2025-69720  ncurses (libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin) 6.5+20250216-2
#   Buffer overflow in ncurses terminal library.
#   seed-job is a one-shot init container that does not use a terminal or any
#   ncurses-linked code path; ncurses is a transitive dep of the Debian base
#   image.  Debian 13 has no fix available yet.  No exploitable path in
#   container context (no TTY, no interactive session).
CVE-2025-69720

# CVE-2026-29111  systemd (libsystemd0, libudev1) 257.9-1~deb13u1
#   Arbitrary code execution / DoS via spurious IPC API call data.
#   seed-job runs as UID 65532 (nonroot) inside a container with no systemd
#   socket mounted; systemd IPC is not reachable from within the container.
#   Debian 13 fix not yet released upstream.
CVE-2026-29111

# CVE-2026-4878   libcap2 1:2.75-10+b8
#   Privilege escalation via TOCTOU race in cap_set_file().
#   seed-job sets no file capabilities and runs as UID 65532 with no
#   CAP_SETFCAP.  No call path to cap_set_file() in the application.
CVE-2026-4878

# ── jaeger-auth (alpine:3.19 + oauth2-proxy v7.6.0 binary + Go stdlib) ───────

# ── Alpine OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# CVE-2026-40200  musl / musl-utils 1.2.4_git20230717-r5
#   Stack-based memory corruption in qsort; arbitrary code execution / DoS.
#   oauth2-proxy is a Go binary; the musl qsort is only reachable by C code.
#   The oauth2-proxy binary is statically linked against Go's runtime, not musl.
#   Alpine 3.19 fix not yet available.
CVE-2026-40200

# ── oauth2-proxy v7.6.0 binary (Go deps bundled) ─────────────────────────────

# CVE-2025-54576  github.com/oauth2-proxy/oauth2-proxy/v7 v7.6.0
#   Authentication bypass in oauth2-proxy.
#   Jaeger UI is internal-only (cluster-internal ingress, not public-facing).
#   Exploitability requires network access to the jaeger-auth service, which is
#   restricted to cluster VPN users.  Upgrade blocked on oauth2-proxy v7.7.x
#   compatibility testing — tracked in issue #MINTKEY-412.
CVE-2025-54576

# CVE-2026-40575  github.com/oauth2-proxy/oauth2-proxy/v7 v7.6.0
#   Authentication bypass via spoofed X-Forwarded-Uri header.
#   Jaeger-auth sits behind Kong, which strips untrusted X-Forwarded-* headers
#   before forwarding.  Internal-only service; mitigated at gateway layer.
CVE-2026-40575

# CVE-2026-34457  github.com/oauth2-proxy/oauth2-proxy/v7 v7.6.0
#   Health-check User-Agent matching bypasses auth in auth_request mode.
#   Mintkey does not use auth_request mode for Jaeger; oauth2-proxy is
#   configured in standalone proxy mode.  No exploitable path.
CVE-2026-34457

# CVE-2026-41059  github.com/oauth2-proxy/oauth2-proxy/v7 v7.6.0
#   Authentication bypass via crafted request path.
#   Jaeger UI only exposes read-only trace data; no privileged actions
#   accessible.  Service is cluster-internal only; external access via VPN.
CVE-2026-41059

# CVE-2025-64484  github.com/oauth2-proxy/oauth2-proxy/v7 v7.6.0
#   Header smuggling via underscore characters; potential privilege escalation.
#   Kong strips headers with underscores at the gateway before reaching
#   jaeger-auth.  Not reachable without gateway bypass.
CVE-2025-64484

# CVE-2024-45337  golang.org/x/crypto v0.18.0
#   Authorization bypass via ServerConfig.PublicKeyCallback misuse.
#   oauth2-proxy does not use PublicKeyCallback; no SSH server is exposed.
CVE-2024-45337

# CVE-2024-24790  stdlib v1.21.7
#   Unexpected behavior from Is methods for IPv4-mapped IPv6 addresses in net/netip.
#   oauth2-proxy upstream dependency; no IPv6 addressing used in Mintkey
#   Jaeger deployment.  Upgrade blocked pending oauth2-proxy release cadence.
CVE-2024-24790

# CVE-2025-68121  stdlib v1.21.7
#   Incorrect certificate validation during TLS session resumption.
#   Jaeger-auth terminates TLS at Kong; internal traffic is mTLS via
#   cert-manager.  TLS session resumption not used on the internal path.
CVE-2025-68121

# CVE-2026-33186  google.golang.org/grpc v1.60.1
#   Authorization bypass in gRPC-Go authz due to improper HTTP/2 path validation.
#   oauth2-proxy does not expose a gRPC endpoint; gRPC is not used in the
#   jaeger-auth service.
CVE-2026-33186

# CVE-2023-45288  stdlib v1.21.7
#   Unlimited CONTINUATION frames in net/http2 causes DoS.
#   oauth2-proxy upstream dependency; HTTP/2 CONTINUATION flood is mitigated at
#   Kong gateway layer (header size limits enforced).
CVE-2023-45288

# CVE-2024-34156  stdlib v1.21.7
#   Stack exhaustion via deeply nested gob structures in encoding/gob.
#   oauth2-proxy does not use gob encoding in any request-handling path.
CVE-2024-34156

# CVE-2025-22868  golang.org/x/oauth2 v0.16.0
#   Unexpected memory consumption during token parsing in oauth2/jws.
#   JWS token sizes are bounded by the IdP (Keycloak); oversized tokens are
#   rejected at ingress.  Not a viable DoS vector in the current deployment.
CVE-2025-22868

# CVE-2025-22869  golang.org/x/crypto v0.18.0
#   DoS in SSH key exchange.
#   oauth2-proxy does not run an SSH server.  No exploitable SSH path.
CVE-2025-22869

# CVE-2025-30204  github.com/golang-jwt/jwt v3.2.2+incompatible
#   Excessive memory allocation during JWT header parsing.
#   JWT size bounded by Keycloak config; oversized tokens blocked at Kong.
CVE-2025-30204

# CVE-2025-47907  stdlib v1.21.7
#   Postgres scan race condition in database/sql.
#   oauth2-proxy does not connect to Postgres; session storage uses Redis.
CVE-2025-47907

# CVE-2025-58183  stdlib v1.21.7
#   Unbounded allocation parsing GNU sparse map in archive/tar.
#   oauth2-proxy processes no tar archives in its request-handling path.
CVE-2025-58183

# CVE-2025-61726  stdlib v1.21.7
#   Memory exhaustion via query parameter parsing in net/url.
#   Kong enforces query string length limits upstream; oversized query strings
#   are rejected before reaching jaeger-auth.
CVE-2025-61726

# CVE-2025-61728  stdlib v1.21.7
#   Excessive CPU consumption building archive index in archive/zip.
#   oauth2-proxy processes no zip archives in its request-handling path.
CVE-2025-61728

# CVE-2025-61729  stdlib v1.21.7
#   DoS via excessive resource consumption through crafted certificate (crypto/x509).
#   Certificates are sourced only from cert-manager / trusted PKI; no
#   user-supplied certificates are accepted.
CVE-2025-61729

# CVE-2026-25679  stdlib v1.21.7
#   Incorrect parsing of IPv6 host literals in net/url.
#   Mintkey Jaeger deployment uses IPv4 only; no IPv6 URLs processed.
CVE-2026-25679

# CVE-2026-32280  stdlib v1.21.7
#   DoS in certificate chain building (crypto/x509 / crypto/tls).
#   Certificates sourced from cert-manager only; no untrusted cert input.
CVE-2026-32280

# CVE-2026-32281  stdlib v1.21.7
#   DoS via inefficient certificate chain validation (crypto/x509).
#   Same mitigation as CVE-2026-32280; cert-manager controls cert inputs.
CVE-2026-32281

# CVE-2026-32283  stdlib v1.21.7
#   DoS via multiple TLS 1.3 key update messages (crypto/tls).
#   Kong terminates external TLS; internal TLS connections are peer-authenticated
#   via mTLS; untrusted clients cannot send raw TLS frames to jaeger-auth.
CVE-2026-32283

# CVE-2026-33811  stdlib v1.21.7
#   DoS via pathological CNAME lookup with cgo DNS resolver.
#   oauth2-proxy is compiled without cgo (standard Go build); cgo DNS resolver
#   is not active.
CVE-2026-33811

# CVE-2026-33814  stdlib v1.21.7
#   Infinite loop processing HTTP/2 SETTINGS frames in transport.
#   Internal service-to-service HTTP/2 is over mTLS with trusted peers only;
#   not reachable by untrusted clients.
CVE-2026-33814

# CVE-2026-34986  github.com/go-jose/go-jose/v3 v3.0.1
#   DoS via crafted JWE object in go-jose.
#   JWE input is sourced from Keycloak tokens only; oversized / malformed JWE
#   blocked at Kong ingress.
CVE-2026-34986

# CVE-2026-39820  stdlib v1.21.7
#   Well-crafted inputs causing panic in ParseAddress/ParseAddressList/ParseList.
#   email address parsing in net/mail; oauth2-proxy does not parse raw email
#   addresses from user-controlled input in this way.
CVE-2026-39820

# CVE-2026-39836  stdlib v1.21.7
#   Panic via NUL byte in net.Dial/LookupPort on Windows.
#   Container runs on Linux (Alpine); Windows-specific code path not active.
CVE-2026-39836

# CVE-2026-42499  stdlib v1.21.7
#   DoS via pathological inputs to consumePhrase in mail address parsing.
#   Same context as CVE-2026-39820; oauth2-proxy does not parse raw RFC 5322
#   addresses from user-controlled input.
CVE-2026-42499

# ── New CVEs added 2026-06-01 (PR #139 CVE-DB flip) — review by 2026-09-01 ──
# These CVEs appeared in the fresh Trivy DB download on 2026-06-01 and affect
# Debian 12/13 base image packages (Perl modules, gnutls, sqlite, zlib, bzip2).
# No fix is available yet for these package versions in the Debian repos.

# CVE-2026-42250  bzip2 (all Debian base images)
#   Off-by-one error in bzip2recover utility.
#   No service uses bzip2recover; it is a standalone recovery tool not invoked
#   by any application code path.  Not exploitable in container context.
CVE-2026-42250

# CVE-2026-48962  perl-IO-Compress (admin-api, mcp-server, admin-ui, seed-job, mock-backend)
#   Arbitrary code execution via attacker-controlled output glob in IO::Compress.
#   None of these services invoke Perl IO::Compress from user-controlled inputs.
#   Perl is a Debian base image transitive dependency only.
CVE-2026-48962

# CVE-2026-48961  IO::Compress (admin-ui, admin-api, mcp-server, seed-job, mock-backend)
#   IO::Compress ships zipdetails binary with path traversal.
#   zipdetails is not invoked by any service.  Debian base image transitive dep.
CVE-2026-48961

# CVE-2026-48959  IO::Uncompress::Unzip (admin-ui, admin-api, mcp-server, seed-job, mock-backend)
#   CPU exhaustion via crafted zip file in IO::Uncompress::Unzip.
#   No service decompresses zip files from user input via Perl.
CVE-2026-48959

# CVE-2025-15649  IO::Uncompress::Unzip (admin-ui, admin-api, mcp-server, seed-job, mock-backend)
#   Propagates uncaught exceptions leading to denial of service.
#   Same context as CVE-2026-48959; Perl not on any user-facing code path.
CVE-2025-15649

# CVE-2026-42496  Archive::Tar (admin-api, mcp-server, admin-ui, seed-job, mock-backend) CRITICAL
#   Archive::Tar before 3.08 extracts symlinks with attacker-controlled targets.
#   No service extracts tar archives from user input; Perl Archive::Tar is a
#   Debian base image transitive dep not invoked in any container code path.
CVE-2026-42496

# CVE-2026-42497  Archive::Tar (admin-api, mcp-server, admin-ui, seed-job, mock-backend) HIGH
#   Archive::Tar before 3.08 extracts hardlinks to attacker-controlled paths.
#   Same context as CVE-2026-42496.
CVE-2026-42497

# CVE-2026-9538  Archive::Tar (admin-api, mcp-server, admin-ui, seed-job, mock-backend) HIGH
#   Archive::Tar before 3.10 allows memory exhaustion via crafted archive.
#   Same context as CVE-2026-42496.
CVE-2026-9538

# CVE-2026-33845  gnutls (admin-api, mcp-server, admin-ui, seed-job, mock-backend) CRITICAL
#   GnuTLS: Denial of Service via DTLS zero-length fragment.
#   None of these services use DTLS; all TLS is standard TLS 1.2/1.3 via Kong.
CVE-2026-33845

# CVE-2026-42010  gnutls (admin-api, mcp-server, admin-ui, seed-job, mock-backend) CRITICAL
#   Authentication bypass via NUL character in username in gnutls.
#   NUL-byte usernames are not a valid input in any Mintkey auth path.
CVE-2026-42010

# CVE-2026-33846  gnutls (admin-api, mcp-server, admin-ui, seed-job, mock-backend) HIGH
#   Heap buffer overflow in DTLS handshake frame processing.
#   Same context as CVE-2026-33845; DTLS not used.
CVE-2026-33846

# CVE-2026-3833  gnutls (admin-api, mcp-server, admin-ui, seed-job, mock-backend) HIGH
#   Policy bypass due to case-sensitive nameConstraints comparison.
#   Certificates are issued by cert-manager / Mintkey PKI; no untrusted certs
#   processed by these services.
CVE-2026-3833

# CVE-2026-42009  gnutls (admin-api, mcp-server, admin-ui, seed-job, mock-backend) HIGH
#   DoS via DTLS packet reordering.
#   Same context as CVE-2026-33845; DTLS not used.
CVE-2026-42009

# CVE-2026-41907  uuid (admin-api, mcp-server, admin-ui, seed-job, mock-backend) HIGH
#   Out-of-bounds write in libuuid / uuid library.
#   The affected e2fsprogs libuuid is a Debian base image dependency not
#   invoked directly by any service application code.
CVE-2026-41907

# CVE-2025-7458  sqlite (admin-api, mcp-server, admin-ui, seed-job, mock-backend) CRITICAL
#   SQLite integer overflow.
#   These services use PostgreSQL, not SQLite.  SQLite is a Debian base image
#   transitive dep that is never loaded or invoked at runtime.
CVE-2025-7458

# CVE-2023-45853  zlib (admin-api, mcp-server, admin-ui, seed-job, mock-backend) CRITICAL
#   Integer overflow in zlib zipOpenNewFileInZip4_64.
#   None of these services create zip archives via zlib's zipOpenNewFileInZip.
#   The minizip API subset affected is not used by any Python package.
CVE-2023-45853

# CVE-2026-8376  perl (admin-api, mcp-server, admin-ui, seed-job, mock-backend) CRITICAL
#   Heap buffer overflow in Perl regex compiler.
#   Perl is a Debian base image dep; none of the Python/Node services execute
#   Perl regexes from user input.  Not exploitable in container context.
CVE-2026-8376

# ── Additional OpenSSL CVEs added 2026-06-01 (second CVE-DB update in same run) ──

# CVE-2026-31789  openssl (all Debian/distroless base images) CRITICAL
#   Heap buffer overflow on 32-bit systems from large X.509 certificate processing.
#   Mintkey containers run on 64-bit Linux only (amd64); the 32-bit overflow code
#   path is not reachable.  No fix available yet in Debian repos.
CVE-2026-31789

# CVE-2026-28387  openssl (all Debian/distroless base images) HIGH
#   Arbitrary code execution due to use-after-free in DANE TLSA authentication.
#   DANE TLSA is not used in Mintkey; TLS is handled by Kong / cert-manager with
#   standard X.509 certificates.
CVE-2026-28387

# CVE-2026-28388  openssl (all Debian/distroless base images) HIGH
#   Denial of Service due to NULL pointer dereference in delta CRL processing.
#   Mintkey does not use delta CRLs; cert revocation is handled by cert-manager
#   with OCSP stapling.
CVE-2026-28388

# CVE-2026-28389  openssl (all Debian/distroless base images) HIGH
#   Denial of Service in CMS processing.
#   Mintkey services do not process CMS (Cryptographic Message Syntax) objects
#   from user-controlled input.
CVE-2026-28389

# CVE-2026-28390  openssl (all Debian/distroless base images) HIGH
#   Denial of Service due to NULL pointer dereference in CMS EnvelopedData.
#   Same context as CVE-2026-28389; CMS not used.
CVE-2026-28390

# CVE-2026-40356  krb5 (libkrb5-3, libkrb5support0, etc. — Debian base images) HIGH
#   MIT Kerberos 5: Denial of Service via integer underflow and out-of-bounds read.
#   Mintkey services do not use Kerberos authentication; krb5 is a Debian base
#   image transitive dependency that is not loaded in any service code path.
CVE-2026-40356

# ── Perl-base CVEs added 2026-06-01 (third CVE-DB flip — IO::Compress / Archive::Tar) ──

# CVE-2026-48962  perl-base (all Debian base images) HIGH
#   IO::Compress: Arbitrary code execution via attacker-controlled output glob in
#   File::GlobMapper._getFiles() eval.
#   Mintkey Python/Node services never invoke IO::Compress / File::GlobMapper from
#   user-supplied input.  perl-base is a Debian base image transitive dependency;
#   no IO::Compress code path is reachable from any service.  No fix available in
#   Debian 12 repos.
CVE-2026-48962

# CVE-2026-9538   perl-base (all Debian base images) HIGH
#   Archive::Tar: Memory exhaustion via crafted tar archive before version 3.10.
#   No Mintkey service processes user-supplied tar archives via Archive::Tar.
#   perl-base is a Debian base image dep that is never loaded at runtime.
CVE-2026-9538

# CVE-2026-42497  perl-base (all Debian base images) HIGH
#   Archive::Tar < 3.08: Hardlink extraction to attacker-controlled paths.
#   No Mintkey service extracts tar archives using Archive::Tar.
#   perl-base is a Debian base image dep that is never loaded at runtime.
CVE-2026-42497

# CVE-2026-42496  perl-base (all Debian base images) CRITICAL
#   Archive::Tar < 3.08: Symlink extraction with attacker-controlled targets.
#   Same mitigation as CVE-2026-42497; no Archive::Tar usage in any service.
CVE-2026-42496

# ── jaeger-auth new stdlib CVEs (PR #139, 2026-06-02) — review by 2026-09-02 ──
# oauth2-proxy v7.15.2 (quay.io/oauth2-proxy/oauth2-proxy:v7.15.2) bundles Go
# stdlib v1.25.9.  These CVEs are fixed in stdlib ≥1.25.10 / ≥1.26.3 but the
# fix requires upgrading to a new oauth2-proxy release (no patch release for
# v7.15.x available).  Upgrade tracked in MINTKEY-412.
# All three are mitigated at the Kong gateway layer before reaching jaeger-auth.

# CVE-2026-39823  stdlib v1.25.9 (jaeger-auth / oauth2-proxy binary) HIGH
#   URL parsing flaw in net/url; attacker-crafted URLs can bypass routing.
#   Kong normalises all URLs before forwarding; jaeger-auth is internal-only
#   and not directly reachable by untrusted clients.
CVE-2026-39823

# CVE-2026-39825  stdlib v1.25.9 (jaeger-auth / oauth2-proxy binary) HIGH
#   ReverseProxy forwards attacker-controlled query strings in net/http/httputil.
#   oauth2-proxy's reverse-proxy mode is only reachable through Kong, which
#   enforces query-string length limits and strips untrusted hop-by-hop headers.
CVE-2026-39825

# CVE-2026-39826  stdlib v1.25.9 (jaeger-auth / oauth2-proxy binary) HIGH
#   Arbitrary JS injection via <script> tag in html/template.
#   oauth2-proxy does not render HTML templates from user-controlled input in
#   Mintkey's deployment; sign-in pages are served by Keycloak, not oauth2-proxy.
CVE-2026-39826

# ── admin-ui build-time npm bundled dep (PR #139, 2026-06-02) — review by 2026-08-01 ──

# CVE-2026-47429  vitest (admin-ui dev-bundle test runner) CRITICAL
#   Exploit requires `vitest --ui` server port exposure to a network
#   attacker. No mintkey workflow runs vitest --ui; operator-only dev
#   tool. Fix is vitest 2→4 major version bump; tracked for a focused
#   migration PR. Dismissed in Dependabot as tolerable_risk on 2026-06-02
#   (alerts #16, #17). Review by 2026-09-01 (quarterly major-bump pass).
CVE-2026-47429

# CVE-2026-33671  picomatch (npm CLI bundled dep) HIGH
#   Affected file: /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/picomatch/package.json
#   This is npm's OWN bundled dependency, not our app's. Our pnpm install uses
#   picomatch@4.0.4 (overridden in apps/admin-ui/package.json `pnpm.overrides`).
#   npm CLI is only used during admin-ui Docker build, never at runtime.
#   Review by 2026-08-01 (next quarterly base-image bump).
CVE-2026-33671

# ── New CVEs 2026-06-20 (PR #229 Go 1.26.4 bump + Playwright fix) — review by 2026-09-20 ──

# CVE-2026-11822  libsqlite3-0 3.40.1-2+deb12u2 (Debian 12 base images) HIGH
#   SQLite <3.53.2 memory corruption.
#   fix_deferred: no Debian 12 fix available. Services use PostgreSQL; libsqlite3
#   is a Debian base image transitive dep never loaded at runtime. Vault-adapter
#   uses the modernc.org/sqlite pure-Go driver, not libsqlite3-0.
CVE-2026-11822

# CVE-2026-11824  libsqlite3-0 3.40.1-2+deb12u2 (Debian 12 base images) HIGH
#   SQLite <3.53.2 heap-based buffer overflow.
#   Same context and mitigation as CVE-2026-11822 above.
CVE-2026-11824

# CVE-2026-45447  libssl3 (Debian 12 base images) HIGH
#   OpenSSL: Heap Use-After-Free in PKCS7_verify(). Fixed in 3.0.20-1~deb12u2.
#   Installed version is 3.0.18-1~deb12u2 or 3.0.20-1~deb12u1 (pre-pin).
#   Mintkey services do not call PKCS7_verify(); TLS is terminated at Kong.
#   Will be resolved in next quarterly base-image re-pin (by 2026-09-20).
CVE-2026-45447

# CVE-2026-12151  undici 6.26.0 (Node.js 26 internally bundled) HIGH
#   Denial of Service via unbounded memory accumulation in undici.
#   admin-ui uses node:26; Node.js 26 bundles undici v6.26.0 internally.
#   Our app's pnpm dependency (from pnpm-lock.yaml) is undici@7.26.0.
#   The bundled internal version cannot be upgraded without a Node.js base
#   image bump (tracked in quarterly base-image re-pin by 2026-09-20).
#   Admin-ui is operator-facing only; not exposed to untrusted clients directly.
CVE-2026-12151

# CVE-2026-6734   undici 6.26.0 (Node.js 26 internally bundled) HIGH
#   Information disclosure and data integrity issue in undici.
#   Same context as CVE-2026-12151; Node.js-bundled undici, not app dep.
CVE-2026-6734

# CVE-2026-9697   undici 6.26.0 (Node.js 26 internally bundled) HIGH
#   Man-in-the-Middle attack via ignored TLS errors in undici.
#   Same context as CVE-2026-12151; internal connection to trusted services only.
CVE-2026-9697
